This dependency-free webhook plugin was generated by PolyPlugin Forge. It binds
to `127.0.0.1` and implements a real `POST /hello` endpoint.

## Verify locally

```bash
npm ci --offline
npm run build
npm test
node dist/server.js
```

Set `PORT=0` to let the operating system select a free port. The server reports
the selected loopback URL on stderr.

Request:

```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:3000/hello \
  -H "content-type: application/json" \
  -d '{"name":"Ada"}'
```

Response:

```json
{"message":"Hello, Ada!"}
```

The package name is `{{packageName}}` and the stable plugin identifier is
`{{pluginId}}`.

## Security and privacy

The server accepts JSON bodies up to 16 KiB, does not persist requests, and
emits no telemetry. It intentionally ships without authentication and must not
be exposed directly to an external network. See `docs/PRIVACY.md`.
